The economic issue is process yield. A blade is purchased repeatedly as its cutting edge wears, but the cost of a failed cut includes downstream inspection, rejects and possible damage to high-value devices. Customers therefore qualify wheel composition, mounting, geometry and bond type under the actual conditions of a device line rather than buying solely on price per blade.

