How Should Manufacturers Choose Cutting Consumables?
A plant should measure cut-edge integrity, kerf width, tool breakage, blade consumption per run and device yield rather than focus only on unit price. For fragile substrates, the chosen bond formulation can change abrasive release and cutting forces. Consistent inventory supply matters when a blade is qualified on a process that cannot readily accept substitutions.

Suppliers seeking design wins need application engineering and evidence from the customer's actual wafer stack. Purchasers should investigate total process cost, including inspection and reject rates, and the degree to which any laser or hybrid alternatives could reduce recurring blade use.

